# Paperclip project rules

This is a native macOS clipboard manager + optional AI Memory (`com.mhadikz.Paperclip`), published as open source (MIT).

## Read first in every new session

1. `README.md`
2. `AGENTS.md`
3. `docs/STATUS.md`
4. Task-specific doc under `docs/` (see `docs/INDEX.md`)

## Architecture

- SwiftUI + MVVM + feature modules + Clean Architecture + DI + Swift Concurrency
- Layers: `App/` · `Features/` · `Domain/` · `Data/` · `Core/`
- Composition root: `Paperclip/App/DependencyContainer.swift` (no new singletons)
- Views → ViewModels → UseCases → Domain protocols; Data implements protocols
- Pure logic lives in `Domain/Services`; AI is reached only via `AIMemoryServicing`
- Write `@ViewState`, never `@State` (Command Line Tools cannot expand the SDK macro)

## Hard invariants

- Capture path must never await AI, OCR, image encoding or disk encoding
- Menu bar clips must ignore History/AI `searchText` (`displayedClips` unfiltered)
- History is a non-activating `NSPanel`; the previous app keeps focus for ⌘V
- Settings open via `PreferencesWindowController` / `AppRouter` (no SwiftUI Settings scene)
- AI is optional; clipboard must work without Foundation Models
- Never log clipboard content / secrets (`AppLogger` only)
- AI metadata is a sidecar — clearing it must keep history
- Duplicate copies bump the existing clip; concealed/transient pasteboard types are skipped

## Build & test

`./scripts/check.sh` (typecheck) · `./scripts/test.sh` (77 tests, no XCTest) · `./scripts/build.sh` (install to `~/Applications`) · `./scripts/render-previews.sh` (UI PNGs). Regenerate the Xcode project with `python3 scripts/generate-xcodeproj.py` after adding files.

## Product stance

Local-only by default. No cloud AI default. No iCloud sync unless explicitly requested. Clipboard-first, not chatbot-first. Add tests for behavior changes; update `docs/STATUS.md` and `CHANGELOG.md`.

## Design

Use `Paperclip/Core/Design/` (`AppTheme`, `AppPalette`, `GlassChrome`). Brand colors only from `AppPalette` (navy/gold/white, Light/Dark). Window glass + interactive chrome; cards/chips are tinted surfaces, not nested `glassEffect`. Glass strength is `AppSettings.glassTintAmount`; appearance is `AppSettings.appearanceMode`. Light tints white, Dark tints midnight. Opaque surfaces when Reduce Transparency is on (`appGlassDisabled`).
